module fluorescence

// NOTE: this excerpt (Figure 3) is a bench-scale miniprep protocol built around
// centrifugation and phase separation, neither of which has a BioScript primitive
// (dispense/mix/heat/detect/repeat/dispose/if is the full available vocabulary). As a
// result, centrifuge_pellet (step 2) and centrifuge_phases_top (step 6) are not modeled;
// the droplet is simply carried forward across these steps. BioScript also has no
// dedicated 'store'/'wait' primitive, so the ON_ICE holds in steps 4-5 are represented
// with 'heat ... at 4c' (the nearest available primitive exposing a temperature and a
// duration) rather than a true storage/wait construct. Steps 7-13 (phenol-chloroform
// extraction and ethanol precipitation) are omitted for brevity in the source paper
// itself and are therefore not modeled here either.

manifest rich_medium
manifest bacteria_colony
manifest lysis_sol1
manifest lysis_sol2
manifest lysis_sol3

instructions:

// Step 1 (Preparation of cells): inoculate rich medium with a single bacterial colony,
// incubate with shaking for 12 hrs at 37 C
medium = dispense 20 units of rich_medium
colony = dispense 1 units of bacteria_colony
culture = mix medium with colony
heat culture at 37c for 720m

// Step 2: measure 1.5 ml of culture into a microfuge tube (the culture droplet already
// represents this aliquot); centrifuge_pellet and supernatant removal are not modeled
// (no centrifugation primitive available)

// Step 3 (Lysis of Cells): add Alkaline Lysis Solution I, resuspend the pellet
sol1 = dispense 1 units of lysis_sol1
lysed1 = mix culture with sol1

// Step 4: add Alkaline Lysis Solution II, invert 5 times, store on ice
sol2 = dispense 1 units of lysis_sol2
lysed2 = mix lysed1 with sol2
heat lysed2 at 4c for 1m

// Step 5: add Alkaline Lysis Solution III, mix by inversion until precipitate stops
// sticking to the tube walls, store on ice for 3-5 min
sol3 = dispense 1 units of lysis_sol3
lysed3 = mix lysed2 with sol3
heat lysed3 at 4c for 5m

// Step 6: centrifuge at max speed, 4 C, 5 min; aspirate the top (aqueous) layer into a
// clean tube and discard the bottom layer -- centrifuge_phases_top is not modeled (no
// phase-separation primitive available)
dispose lysed3
